   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <dateline>
                    <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI">Paris</name> <date when="1934-04-24">April the 24-th.1934</date>
                </dateline>
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="gads84">John Gadsby</name> esq. C.B.E.</addrLine>
                            <addrLine>Building N<hi rend="superscript">o</hi>13</addrLine>
                            <addrLine>N<hi rend="superscript">o</hi>12 Marunouchi 2-Chome</addrLine>
                            <addrLine>Kojimachi-Ku</addrLine> <addrLine>Tokyo.</addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab>
                </div>
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <opener>
                        <salute>Dear Sir,</salute>
                    </opener>
                    <p>I beg to acknowledge hereby receipt of your favour of the <date when="1934-03-26">26-th.of March</date> <choice>
                            <sic>contaning</sic>
                            <corr>containing</corr>
                        </choice> a cheque for the equivalent of 400 yen representing the proceeds of <name type="person" key="joyc82">Mr Joyce</name>’s claim against the <choice>
                            <sic>japanese</sic>
                            <corr>Japanese</corr>
                        </choice> pirates.</p>
                    <p>I enclose Mr Joyce’s <rs type="letter" key="L_71750">receipt</rs> for it.</p>
                    <p>Let me thank you for your handling of this affair and the results which under the circumstances I understand could not have been better.</p>
                    <p>I fully agree with the wording of your receipt.</p>
                    <p>Will you please thank <name type="organisation" key="ID_MISSING">H.B.M.’s Consul</name> for his intervention as well as <name type="person" key="okak68">Prof. Okakura</name> who has done his best to bring about this understanding.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>Believe me</salute>
                        <salute>sincerely yours.</salute>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="global-note1" type="global">This letter has been transcribed from a typed carbon copy. It was sent as an enclosure with the <rs type="letter" key="L_71750">letter from Paul Léon of 24 April 1934</rs>.</note>
            </div>  
